WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:07.142
Nine twelve p.m. Sunita's phone rings. It is her son, crying for help.

2
00:00:08.142 --> 00:00:14.799
Then a man says he is a police officer. Pay fifty thousand rupees now, and tell no one.

3
00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:17.788
Let's look at the evidence.

4
00:00:18.588 --> 00:00:24.850
Exhibit one: the voice. A few seconds from a video he posted were enough to copy it.

5
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:31.873
Exhibit two: the number. It is not her son's number, and it is not a police station.

6
00:00:32.673 --> 00:00:38.995
Exhibit three: the demand. Urgency, money and secrecy, all in one call.

7
00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:44.855
Sunita hangs up, and calls her son back on the number she already has saved.

8
00:00:46.455 --> 00:00:50.080
He picks up. He is safe, in class.

9
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:58.694
It was a voice clone. Deepfakes can copy a face or a voice from just a few seconds of video.

10
00:00:59.494 --> 00:01:04.147
So agree on a family safe word, and always call back on the saved number.

11
00:01:04.947 --> 00:01:12.668
Before you forward a shocking video, check it with a fact checker. Verify first. Forward never.

12
00:01:13.468 --> 00:01:19.484
If it happens to you, call one nine three zero, or report on cybercrime dot gov dot in.
